vms-fastfetch for OpenVMS
=========================

A fastfetch-compatible system information tool: a logo and lines of
system details (OS, host, CPU, memory, disks, network, packages, ...),
read from OpenVMS system services.  Runs on OpenVMS x86-64 and IA64.

Setup
-----
After PRODUCT INSTALL FASTFETCH:

  At system startup (SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM):
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:FASTFETCH$STARTUP.COM
  For each user (LOGIN.COM, or SYS$MANAGER:SYLOGIN.COM for everyone):
    $ @FASTFETCH$ROOT:[000000]FASTFETCH$SETUP.COM

Use
---
  $ fastfetch                          ! the default banner
  $ fastfetch -c all                   ! every supported module
  $ fastfetch -c ci                    ! plain text, for batch logs
  $ fastfetch -s os:cpu:memory -l none ! chosen modules, no logo
  $ fastfetch --format json            ! results as JSON
  $ fastfetch --list-modules
  $ fastfetch -h

Options are case-insensitive.  Quote format strings to keep their case
and spaces:
  $ fastfetch -s disk --disk-format "{size-percentage} {filesystem}"

Configuration
-------------
fastfetch's JSONC config format, read from (first found):
  - the file named by the logical name FASTFETCH$CONFIG
  - [<login>.^.config.fastfetch]config.jsonc (fastfetch's ~/.config/fastfetch)
  - SYS$LOGIN:FASTFETCH.JSONC
"fastfetch --gen-config" writes a starting config to the second location.
FASTFETCH$ROOT:[DOC]CONFIG.MD lists the keys, options and format arguments.

Terminals
---------
Colours are used when SYS$OUTPUT is a terminal; --pipe or the NO_COLOR
logical name turns them off.  Logos are ASCII, for DECterm and VT terminals.

